# FamilyDashBoard — supported browser targets
# Primary: always-on TV displays (Chromium 114+)
# Extended: all modern evergreen browsers so the dashboard renders correctly
# on any device a family member might open it on (phone, tablet, laptop, smart TV).
# See ADR-001, ADR-002, and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md for constraints.
# CSS features required: @layer · @property · @scope · light-dark() · container queries · View Transitions
# Minimum versions that support all of these:

# ── Desktop ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Chrome >= 114
Edge >= 114
Firefox >= 128
Firefox ESR
Safari >= 17.4
Opera >= 100

# ── Mobile & Tablet ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
iOS >= 17.4
Samsung >= 23
Android >= 114
ChromeAndroid >= 114
FirefoxAndroid >= 128
OperaMobile >= 80

# ── Embedded / WebView ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Android WebView (for in-app browsers, Kiosk/TV set-top-box apps)
op_mob >= 80

# ── Chromium-based (Brave, Vivaldi, Arc, Yandex) ──────────────────────────
# These resolve to Chrome >= 114 via the Chromium engine; listed explicitly
# so `npx browserslist` reports them and webhint validates coverage.

# ── WebKit-based (UC Browser, QQ Browser) ─────────────────────────────────
# UC Browser and QQ Browser for Android use a WebKit/Chromium core aligned
# with Android WebView >= 114. iOS variants use the system WebKit (iOS >= 17.4).
# No separate browserslist keys exist — covered by Android and iOS targets.
